Passion Fruit Posset [
	• Total time ~10 min active + 4 hr chill.
	Ingredients [
		• Heavy cream — 2 cups (480 ml, 36%+ fat req)
		• Sugar — 2/3 cup (130 g)
		• Passion fruit pulp — 1/3 cup (~6 fresh fruit, or frozen pulp)
		• Salt — pinch
	]

	Method [

		Reduce [
			• Cream + sugar + salt → saucepan, medium heat.
			• Stir til sugar dissolved.
			• Bring to gentle boil. Boil 3 min exactly, stirring.
			• Watch it. Boils over fast.
		]

		Acidify [
			• Off heat.
			• Strain passion pulp if you want smooth (keep seeds for crunch — both work).
			• Whisk passion juice into cream.
			• Mix curdles slightly = correct.
		]

		Set [
			• Cool 15 min on counter.
			• Cover, fridge 4+ hrs (overnight better).
		]
	]

	Serve [
		• Top w/ extra passion pulp + seeds for color & crunch.
	]

	Troubleshooting [
		• Won't set ⇒ cream fat too low, OR boiled <3 min, OR not enough acid
		• Too tart ⇒ +1 tbsp sugar next time
		• Grainy ⇒ sugar didn't dissolve pre-boil
	]
]